      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Pub/Sub Provider**\n\nI've decided to use Google Cloud Pub/Sub as the external provider. I'm planning to implement the `consume_event.py` script using the Google Cloud Pub/Sub client library. This approach allows me to access a single message from the queue or subscription.\n\n\n**Defining Message Consumption Logic**\n\nI'm now focused on the specific logic for `consume_event.py`. I'm committed to using Google Cloud Pub/Sub and its client library, ensuring that it can pull one message at a time. This approach will allow for cleaner access to the queue. I will include signals in the code, so that it will show the use of `google.cloud.pubsub_v1`.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861412430,
          "start": 1789861409922
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc0db4820011XMfd5fDW6yeQm",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc0db0cd001G7VGGmFBdtpMnr",
      "session_id": "ses_f43f24f42ffeWFbLfWyZ1zyCd0",
      "time_created": 1789861409922,
      "time_updated": 1789861412430
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "oSEnxdCugu72kzJF",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import pubsub_v1\nimport os\n\ndef consume_event(project_id: str, subscription_id: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Consumes one message from a Google Cloud Pub/Sub subscription.\n\n    Args:\n        project_id: The Google Cloud project ID.\n        subscription_id: The ID of the Pub/Sub subscription.\n\n    Returns:\n        A dictionary containing the message data and attributes, or None if no message is received.\n    \"\"\"\n    subscriber = pubsub_v1.SubscriberClient()\n    subscription_path = subscriber.subscription_path(project_id, subscription_id)\n\n    response = subscriber.pull(\n        request={\"subscription\": subscription_path, \"max_messages\": 1, \"return_immediately\": True},\n        timeout=5.0  # Optional: set a timeout for the pull request\n    )\n\n    if response.received_messages:\n        message = response.received_messages[0].message\n        subscriber.acknowledge(\n            request={\"subscription\": subscription_path, \"ack_ids\": [response.received_messages[0].ack_id]}\n        )\n        return {\n            \"data\": message.data.decode(\"utf-8\"),\n            \"attributes\": dict(message.attributes)\n        }\n    return None\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Replace with your actual Google Cloud project ID and subscription ID\n    project_id = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT\")\n    subscription_id = os.environ.get(\"PUBSUB_SUBSCRIPTION_ID\")\n\n    if not project_id or not subscription_id:\n        print(\"Please set GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT and PUBSUB_SUBSCRIPTION_ID environment variables.\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"Attempting to consume message from subscription: {subscription_id} in project: {project_id}\")\n        message = consume_event(project_id, subscription_id)\n        if message:\n            print(\"Received message:\")\n            print(f\"Data: {message['data']}\")\n            print(f\"Attributes: {message['attributes']}\")\n        else:\n            print(\"No messages received.\")\n",
            "filePath": "consume_event.py"
          },
